<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who the Luxury Series is for</h2>
        <p>Nordic's Luxury Series is for families who want a feature-rich, full-size spa at a value price. All three models seat six to eight, and they pair corner captain's chairs and No-Float loungers with Nordic Star stainless steel jets. The 6-person Encore LS, for example, has 53 jets driven by a 3 hp two-speed pump and a 2 hp pump, plus the Northern Lighting Package (LED waterfall, sconce, jet and cup-holder lighting) as standard.</p>
        <h2>Electrical and installation</h2>
        <p>Luxury Series spas are 220/240V spas. Nordic lists the Encore LS at 220V/50A with a 4 kW heater, so you'll need a dedicated circuit from a licensed electrician. The Encore LS is 84 × 84 inches, 35 inches deep, and holds about 330 gallons. Plan a level pad or engineered deck rated for a filled spa with six adults in it. See our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-cost-utah/">Utah cost guide</a> for typical installation costs.</p>
        <h2>The Luxury Series in a Utah winter</h2>
        <p>Nordic's standard foam insulation can be upgraded with <strong>Nordic Wrap</strong>, which the manufacturer says adds R-9.5 for low ambient temperatures. For Wasatch Front winters, especially on the benches, it's worth considering. Add a tight-fitting <a href="/covers/">cover</a> and see our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">winter guide</a>.</p>
        <h2>See Nordic in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit. Compare Nordic with our Artesian lines in our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-brands-compared/">brand comparison</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

